      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Overview** combines all Fastify pods. **Pods (details)** filters only the per-pod section; choose one, several, or All. The selector includes pods observed in the selected time range. A one-hour chart may contain three pod names even when only two pods run now: the third is a replaced pod's history. Current scrape health uses an instant query; history uses a range query.\n\n**UP means the metrics endpoint can be scraped.** It does not prove application readiness or a correct redirect. Target counts do not track desired Kubernetes replicas: a removed target disappears rather than staying DOWN. Kubernetes readiness and end-to-end checks are separate signals.\n\nRun **`pnpm load:demo`** for 100 → 500 → 1,000 → 100 redirects/s, plus one GraphQL creation/s. Five percent deliberately request missing codes. Prometheus scrapes every **5 seconds**; rates and histogram percentiles use **30-second windows**. Quiet periods have no meaningful latency percentile, and new counters need baseline samples. The latency reference is **100 ms of server time**; our performance target uses client measurements. Pool gauges can miss short spikes. HTTP `200` may contain GraphQL errors.\n\nDashboard and datasource are provisioned from repository files. Local history is retained for up to **24 hours / 256 MB**."
      }
    }
